# diff — real-world examples

## Differences between two files (unified format)

```sh
diff -u version1 version2
```

## Differences between two directories, recursively

```sh
diff -ur folder1/ folder2/
```

## Ignore whitespace / blank lines / case

```sh
diff -ub version1 version2   # ignore whitespace changes
diff -uB version1 version2   # ignore blank lines
diff -ui version1 version2   # ignore case
```

## Just tell me whether they differ

```sh
diff -q version1 version2    # reports if different
diff -s version1 version2    # reports if identical
```

## Diff the output of two commands (process substitution)

```sh
diff <(command1) <(command2)
```

## Homelab: compare live config against the backup

```sh
diff -u /etc/nginx/nginx.conf ~/backups/etc/nginx/nginx.conf
```

## Homelab: what changed between two package snapshots

```sh
diff <(ssh david@homelab 'rpm -qa | sort') <(rpm -qa | sort)
```

| Flag | What it does                    |
| ---- | ------------------------------- |
| -u   | unified format (patch-friendly) |
| -r   | recurse into directories        |
| -q   | brief: only "files differ"      |
| -s   | report identical files          |
| -b   | ignore whitespace changes       |
| -B   | ignore blank lines              |
| -i   | ignore case                     |
